  "patch_scope": "fast_graph replaces process-global core.Tracer.sharding property with a cheaper AttributeError only for the load_model context, restoring original in finally. Normal loader also temporarily wraps nnx.eval_shape for graph timing and restores it in finally. Scope is whole load_model, not solely graph_build. No device executable or inference-step patch. This is not a thread-local patch or a general concurrent-initializer safety proof.",
  "timers": "graph_build times nnx.eval_shape of model constructor, nested within load_model. Normal graph timer excludes checkpoint loading. load_model excludes subsequent precision inspection, cache initialization and warm-up. Restore remains sequential SHA verify then abstract graph then validation/placement/update; unused overlap helpers are not evidence of overlap in this campaign.",
  "lifecycle": "Each arm newly creates four instances/eight workers; prior arm release precedes next initialization. Each arm drain removes four actors and placement groups. Eight tmpfs directories are empty after final cleanup.",
  "checksum_distinction": "Both restore arms use older v1 full-SHA path, not FastSnapshot v2 checksum_kind=none. verified_checksums alone is a requested-setting field; successful restored status plus inspected v1 prepare loop supports actual verification. No per-shard fingerprint dump is claimed for this campaign.",
  "confounds": [
    "One fixed-order S sequence: normal-base, normal-fast, restore-base, restore-fast.",
    "cold label means normal checkpoint loader, not cold filesystem or compilation caches.",
    "Snapshot files are created after first arm; normal-fast runs with snapshots resident unlike normal-base.",
    "Eight worker clocks are correlated and concurrent, not eight independent trials or additive savings.",
    "Total-load differences are observations, not fully isolated causal estimates; no confidence interval.",
    "Standalone branch does not combine FastSnapshot, corrected threshold, or production overlap changes."
  ],
